<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xizong of Jin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1119">1119</a>–1150</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wanyan Hela</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xizong of Jin, personal name Wanyan Hela, was the third emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchen-jin-dynasty">Jurchen Jin dynasty</a>, reigning from 1135 to 1150. A grandson of the founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-jin">Aguda</a>, educated in Chinese learning, he centralised government on Tang and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> models, curbing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> princes, and in 1141 concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-shaoxing">Treaty of Shaoxing</a> with the Southern Song. Increasingly violent in later years, he was murdered in 1150 by his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wanyan-liang">Wanyan Liang</a>.</p></div>
